1. Inspection results: /workspace contains only task.json; no project repository, no Megatron/DeepSpeed/Zhongkui code, no torch, no GPU (nvidia-smi fails), network disabled. Therefore all code-level claims are cited from upstream knowledge + the task's hints and are explicitly marked as assumptions to be verified in the first design step (grep verification of argparse).

Known upstream facts (flagged as unverified here):
- Flags documented in the ZB paper (arXiv 2401.10167, "Zero Bubble Pipeline Parallelism"): 1F1B, interleaved 1F1B, DGP, ZB-1p, ZB-2p, ZB-H, with ZB-H activated via --zb-hiv / an update-priority flag. ZB-1p/ZB-2p are activated by setting max pending B to p × the number of microbatches. Actual precise info: ZB-1p: max pending B = number of stages; ZB-2p: 2× the number of stages; ZB-H: --zb-hiv true, --zb-hiv-ub true.
